UP 510: Plan Making Workshop is a central component for the training of urban planning professionals in the MUP Program. The workshop is structured to support students in developing professional experience by learning through practice.


Students in this workshop will:

Become familiar with the purpose and uses of comprehensive plan making;
Apply concepts and skills from prior courses to the practice of plan making;
Engage with the local community to make a meaningful contribution to ongoing planning efforts;
Develop perspective and skills associated with professional practice as an urban planner.




This is a workshop class. Consequently most class sessions will be run as a team staff meeting, and will include flexible time for work. We will spend some time in the first few weeks building shared background and goal setting for tasks to be completed during the remainder of the semester. These tasks will be group efforts and will require engagement and leadership in project management and producing a quality work product for our client to adopt and use. As students working on a “real world” planning process, expect to spend time outside of class accomplishing the plan making tasks.

